This is a miscompilation bug in SLPVectorizer.
Issue title: [SLPVectorizer] Miscompile in slp vectorizer (shift produces poison)
Detailed information:
BUG TYPE:
    miscompilation

VERIFICATION RESULT:
    Invalid refinement in @test -- Source is more defined than target

VIOLATED PROPERTY:
    UB refinement

SOURCE (pre-transformation IR):
target datalayout = "e-m:e-p270:32:32-p271:32:32-p272:64:64-i64:64-i128:128-f80:128-n8:16:32:64-S128"
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu"
define float @test(i8 %0) {
entry:
  %1 = sext i8 0 to i32
  %2 = lshr i32 %1, 27
  %3 = sext i8 %0 to i32
  %reass.add.epil = mul i32 %3, 2
  %4 = or i32 %reass.add.epil, %2
  switch i32 %4, label %exit [
    i32 0, label %exit
    i32 1, label %exit
  ]
exit:                                             ; preds = %entry, %entry, %entry
  ret float 0.000000e+00
}

TARGET (post-transformation IR):
; ModuleID = '<stdin>'
source_filename = "<stdin>"
target datalayout = "e-m:e-p270:32:32-p271:32:32-p272:64:64-i64:64-i128:128-f80:128-n8:16:32:64-S128"
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu"

define float @test(i8 %0) {
entry:
  %1 = insertelement <2 x i8> <i8 poison, i8 0>, i8 %0, i32 0
  %2 = sext <2 x i8> %1 to <2 x i16>
  %3 = mul <2 x i16> %2, <i16 2, i16 27>
  %4 = lshr <2 x i16> %2, <i16 2, i16 27>
  %5 = shufflevector <2 x i16> %3, <2 x i16> %4, <2 x i32> <i32 0, i32 3>
  %6 = extractelement <2 x i16> %5, i32 0
  %7 = sext i16 %6 to i32
  %8 = extractelement <2 x i16> %5, i32 1
  %9 = zext i16 %8 to i32
  %10 = or i32 %7, %9
  switch i32 %10, label %exit [
    i32 0, label %exit
    i32 1, label %exit
  ]
exit:                                             ; preds = %entry, %entry, %entry
  ret float 0.000000e+00
}

WHAT THE TRANSFORMATION CHANGED:
  modified:
    %1
      source: %1 = sext i8 0 to i32
      target: %1 = insertelement <2 x i8> <i8 poison, i8 0>, i8 %0, i32 0
    %2
      source: %2 = lshr i32 %1, 27
      target: %2 = sext <2 x i8> %1 to <2 x i16>
    %3
      source: %3 = sext i8 %0 to i32
      target: %3 = mul <2 x i16> %2, <i16 2, i16 27>
    %4
      source: %4 = or i32 %reass.add.epil, %2
      target: %4 = lshr <2 x i16> %2, <i16 2, i16 27>
  only in target:
    %5: %5 = shufflevector <2 x i16> %3, <2 x i16> %4, <2 x i32> <i32 0, i32 3>
    %6: %6 = extractelement <2 x i16> %5, i32 0
    %7: %7 = sext i16 %6 to i32
    %8: %8 = extractelement <2 x i16> %5, i32 1
    %9: %9 = zext i16 %8 to i32
    %10: %10 = or i32 %7, %9
  only in source:
    %reass.add.epil: %reass.add.epil = mul i32 %3, 2

CRITICAL VALUES:
    %reass.add.epil

DEPENDENCY CHAIN (source):
    %3 = sext i8 %0 to i32
    %reass.add.epil = mul i32 %3, 2

CONTROL FLOW (blocks entered by the failing execution):
    %exit

COUNTEREXAMPLE INPUT:
    (none)

DIVERGENCE (source vs target on that input):
    (none)

INTERPRETATION:
    A transformation may not introduce undefined behaviour. Any execution that is UB-free in the source must remain UB-free in the target.

